{"title":"Career Roadmap: Dietitian Assistant","role":"Dietitian Assistant","summary":"A Dietitian Assistant supports qualified dietitians and nutrition professionals in areas such as:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Food Science & Nutrition"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build foundations in nutrition, food science, diet planning, nutritional assessment, food safety and clinical nutrition support"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Dietitian Assistant supports qualified dietitians and nutrition professionals in areas such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nutrition assessment support"},{"text":"Diet-plan preparation"},{"text":"Meal planning"},{"text":"Patient/client records"},{"text":"Food analysis"},{"text":"Dietary education"},{"text":"Hospital food-service coordination"},{"text":"Nutrition research"},{"text":"Community nutrition programs"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["The role requires a combination of nutrition science","food science","communication","documentation","practical diet-planning skills."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Dietitian Assistant” is distinct from independently practicing as a Registered Dietitian / Dietitian. In India, professional eligibility and title requirements can vary by employer and applicable regulations. A B.Sc. alone should not be presented as automatically authorizing independent clinical dietetic practice."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Nutrition & food foundations"},{"text":"Biology, chemistry, food science"},{"text":"Food/nutrition portfolio"},{"text":"Weak science fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Nutritional science"},{"text":"Macronutrients, micronutrients, physiology"},{"text":"Nutritional analysis project"},{"text":"Memorizing nutrients only"}],[{"text":"3rd Year"},{"text":"Dietetics support skills"},{"text":"Clinical/community nutrition, assessment"},{"text":"Sample diet-planning portfolio"},{"text":"No practical exposure"}],[{"text":"Final Year"},{"text":"Professional readiness"},{"text":"Food service, documentation, counseling support"},{"text":"Internship + capstone"},{"text":"Confusing assistant role with independent practice"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 1–2 — Food & Biological Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human biology"},{"text":"Basic anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"General chemistry"},{"text":"Food science fundamentals"},{"text":"Introduction to nutrition"},{"text":"Food microbiology"},{"text":"Basic statistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digestion"},{"text":"Absorption"},{"text":"Metabolism"},{"text":"Energy balance"},{"text":"Macronutrients"},{"text":"Micronutrients"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 3–4 — Nutrition Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human nutrition"},{"text":"Macronutrients"},{"text":"Micronutrients"},{"text":"Nutritional biochemistry"},{"text":"Food chemistry"},{"text":"Food microbiology"},{"text":"Food preservation"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Food safety"},{"text":"Nutritional requirements"},{"text":"Life-cycle nutrition"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Study nutrition across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Infants"},{"text":"Children"},{"text":"Adolescents"},{"text":"Adults"},{"text":"Older adults"},{"text":"Pregnancy and lactation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 5–6 — Dietetics & Applied Nutrition"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical nutrition fundamentals"},{"text":"Therapeutic diets"},{"tex